WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.969
Why do we see leaves as green and fire

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.889
trucks as red? When we look at most

00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:13.049
objects, they appear colored because

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:15.629
radiation from the Sun bounces off them

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:17.670
in light waves called photons. Photons

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:20.790
scatter off objects and are received by

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:24.180
our eyes. But when you watch TV, where do

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:26.040
the colors come from? Today, colors on

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.350
most TV screens come from a series of

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.660
tiny lamps called light-emitting diodes

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:33.480
or LEDs.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:36.570
These LEDs emit three basic colors: red

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.790
green, and blue. In order to make other

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.060
colors, the LEDs combine these three

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.950
colors in various proportions.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.989
Since LEDs emit three colors with broad

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.660
color profiles, they can struggle to

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:50.250
represent colors with high-precision.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:52.050
Quantum dots, on the other hand,  are a new

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.750
technology capable of emitting colors

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.640
much more accurately. Scientists hope to

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.620
fine tune the distribution of colors so

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.270
that the blue becomes bluer, the green

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.180
becomes greener and the red becomes

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:04.860
redder! Quantum dots are microscopic: the

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.420
size of a quantum dot relative to a

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.819
human is like the size of a human

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.740
relative to the Sun! They are made from

00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:12.229
materials called semiconductors which

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.280
have special properties.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.560
Semiconductors have energy bands that

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.270
electrons can move between. When a photon

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.399
hits an electron, the electron absorbs

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.770
the photon's energy and jumps to a higher

00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:25.020
energy band. To relax to a lower energy

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.240
band, the electron can release a photon

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:28.679
that matches the energy difference. This

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.659
means the difference between the two

00:01:28.679 --> 00:01:32.759
energy levels determines the energy of

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:35.009
the photon released, which is related to

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.719
the color of the light. Scientists can

00:01:35.009 --> 00:01:38.099
alter the size of the quantum dots to

00:01:36.719 --> 00:01:40.139
fine-tune the energy difference between

00:01:38.099 --> 00:01:42.599
the two bands and change the color of

00:01:40.139 --> 00:01:44.189
the light emitted by the dot. Smaller

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:46.649
dots actually have a larger energy

00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:48.060
difference between energy bands. To get

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:50.399
all the way back down to the lower

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.499
energy band, electrons must emit a photon

00:01:50.399 --> 00:01:54.829
with high energy, creating colors with

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:56.849
short wavelengths, like blue or violet.

00:01:54.829 --> 00:01:59.159
Larger dots have smaller energy

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.929
differences between bands. These large

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:02.700
dots give off a lower energy light with

00:02:00.929 --> 00:02:05.609
longer wavelengths, creating hues of

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.469
yellow or red. Scientists have been

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:09.720
working hard to create quantum dots with

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:12.300
high efficiency. For every photon these

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.070
quantum dots absorb, several photons of

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.650
the quantum dot's specific color come

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.790
back out. Many newer TVs today use

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.500
quantum dots because they

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.689
produce more pure color in a more

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.750
energy-efficient way than LEDs used in

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:26.579
conventional TVs. However, quantum dots

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:29.040
could be used in much more than just TV

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:31.049
screens! With more precise colors,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.760
astronomers could collect more accurate

00:02:31.049 --> 00:02:34.950
data about the spectra of light coming

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.629
from distant stars, giving more exact

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.659
readings of the object's age and

00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:41.250
composition. In addition, quantum dots can

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.680
be used to harvest sunlight and convert

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:45.450
it into electricity. Scientists are also

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.090
using quantum dots to develop better

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.769
methods of medical imaging. Quantum dots

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:51.930
could improve on the current technology of

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:53.790
using dyes or other imaging agents to

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:55.590
visualize cancer tumors by providing a

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:58.409
better delineation between cancerous

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.480
tissues and other tissues. Surgeons could

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:01.919
operate with greater precision, helping

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.379
preserve a patient's healthy tissue.

00:03:01.919 --> 00:03:06.480
However, more research needs to be done

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:08.790
to determine if quantum dots are safe to

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.189
use in humans. One advantage of using

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:13.129
quantum dots as their small size, which

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:15.510
allows them to be dispersed in liquids.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:17.819
Therefore, many liquid processing

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:19.680
techniques, such as inkjet printing and

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:22.500
spin-coating, can be applied when using

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.209
quantum dots. This allows quantum dots to

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.180
be integrated into products quickly,

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:29.099
easily and at a low cost. Quantum dots

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.409
are a new microscopic technology for

00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:33.030
emitting colored light. These tiny lights

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:35.069
excite scientists because they are

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:37.290
designed to emit highly specific colors

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:39.419
in a very efficient way paving the way,

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.790
paving the way for more vivid,  lifelike displays. In the

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.930
near future, there's a good chance your

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:45.690
cellphone screen could be made from

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:48.979
quantum dots! Soon quantum dot technology

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.979
will color our lives!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.680
 

